// Cycles and tempo
// Music here happens in cycles:
// loops of equal length. The words
// in quotes split one cycle into
// equal steps.
//
// Try: play, then add or remove
// words. One word fills the whole
// cycle; eight words make eighths.

setcpm(30)
$: s("bd sd bd sd")
// ---
// Tempo
// setcpm sets how many cycles play
// in a minute. 30 cycles of 4 beats
// make 120 beats per minute.
//
// Try: change 30 into 35, then into
// 20, and Update each time.

setcpm(30)
$: s("bd sd bd sd")
$: s("hh hh hh hh hh hh hh hh")
  .gain(0.5)
// ---
// Rests
// ~ is a step where nothing plays.
//
// Try: move the cp to another step,
// add a second cp, or put a ~ in
// place of a bd.

setcpm(30)
$: s("bd ~ bd ~")
$: s("~ ~ cp ~")
// ---
// Steps of different sizes
// Each layer splits the cycle on its
// own: 3 steps against 4 make a
// rhythm that pulls.
//
// Try: change how many words a line
// has (2, 5, 7...) and listen to how
// the layers meet.

setcpm(30)
$: s("bd bd bd bd")
$: s("cp cp cp").gain(0.6)
// ---
// Faster and slower
// .fast(2) plays the whole pattern
// twice in a cycle; .slow(2) spreads
// it over two cycles.
//
// Try: 1.5, 3, 0.5 instead of 2.
// Lesson 5: mini-notation, the small
// language inside the quotes.

setcpm(30)
$: s("bd sd").fast(2)
$: note("c3 e3 g3 b3")
  .s("piano").slow(2)
